From: Jack Wang <jinpu.wang@cloud.ionos.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 12:37:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] md: fix mddev_unlock() called without holding lock in
 lbs_store()
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.3.6
Git-commit: 68dab5c14aaff17686df22ba1f1eea3b3433797a

[ Upstream commit 68dab5c14aaff17686df22ba1f1eea3b3433797a ]

lbs_store() jumped to the unlock label on mddev_lock() failure,
calling mddev_unlock() on a mutex that was never acquired. Return
directly instead.

Fixes: 62ed1b582246 ("md: allow configuring logical block size")
Signed-off-by: Jack Wang <jinpu.wang@cloud.ionos.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260920103705.23191-1-jinpu.wang@ionos.com
Signed-off-by: Yu Kuai <yukuai@fygo.io>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/md/md.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/md/md.c b/drivers/md/md.c
index ef46a7ffeddd..8c56c521a8f8 100644
--- a/drivers/md/md.c
+++ b/drivers/md/md.c
@@ -6051,11 +6051,10 @@ lbs_store(struct mddev *mddev, const char *buf, size_t len)
 
 	err = mddev_lock(mddev);
 	if (err)
-		goto unlock;
+		return err;
 
 	err = mddev_set_logical_block_size(mddev, lbs);
 
-unlock:
 	mddev_unlock(mddev);
 	return err ?: len;
 }
-- 
2.56.1

